// inlines (before config.js). index.html never loads it, loadGameSource() and
// the service worker never list it: it is the second deliberate exception to
// the four-places rule, next to js/portable.js.
//
// Launch handoff. When an earlier run cached a newer, signed build in
// IndexedDB (js/portable.js stores it), this opens that build instead of the
// embedded one:
//  - it runs only in the top window, without ?noupdate, and when the
//    lp_update_ready pointer is newer than the embedded version and not on
//    the bad list;
//  - it re-verifies the cached record's ECDSA signature on every launch;
//  - the portable onload wrapper (js/portable.js) awaits `ready`, and on a
//    result calls mount(): a full-viewport srcdoc iframe. srcdoc inherits this
//    file's origin, so the lp_ saves are shared. (document.write was rejected:
//    re-evaluating top-level consts in one window throws.)
//  - crash guard: mount() sets lp_update_booting to 'version@time'; the child
//    clears it once its PortableUI initialises. A marker still set at the next
//    launch AND older than BOOT_WINDOW_MS means that version never came up: it
//    goes on the bad list, its cache is deleted and the embedded build boots.
//    A younger marker is a boot still in flight (a second tab opened during
//    it) or a tab closed early, so it is ignored: nothing is bad-listed or
//    deleted. mount() keeps the first timestamp of a young marker for the same
//    version, so a crash loop still goes stale and is caught.
// Every failure resolves null, which boots the embedded build, silently.
//
// The two double-underscore placeholders are replaced by the build. It cannot
// read config.js constants (it runs before them), so the key is injected. The
// literals below mirror js/portable.js; tests/test_portable_launch.js drives
// both ends against each other.

